WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.172
Three simple code lookups.

2
00:00:02.372 --> 00:00:05.522
Four turns. 294k tokens.

3
00:00:05.722 --> 00:00:09.794
Every turn, an AI coding agent
reads its whole conversation again.

4
00:00:10.411 --> 00:00:14.111
Now the same lookups, with
PeterGanuRusty, PGR for short.

5
00:00:14.311 --> 00:00:16.223
One question. One answer.

6
00:00:16.423 --> 00:00:19.687
The stream shortens to 134k tokens.

7
00:00:19.887 --> 00:00:22.791
54% fewer than no index, in 2 turns.

8
00:00:22.991 --> 00:00:26.735
That is one comparison:
Claude Haiku 5.5, low effort,

9
00:00:26.735 --> 00:00:28.122
first question set.

10
00:00:28.858 --> 00:00:31.185
It is a command-line
program for the desktop.

11
00:00:31.225 --> 00:00:34.830
AI coding agents call it to look
things up in the code they work on.

12
00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:37.208
It runs on your machine, with no account.

13
00:00:37.666 --> 00:00:39.245
It gives an agent four things.

14
00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:42.713
Where a function is defined,
and what calls it, in one lookup.

15
00:00:42.767 --> 00:00:45.693
Search by meaning: describe
a job, get the function.

16
00:00:45.953 --> 00:00:48.006
What a change reaches, before the edit.

17
00:00:48.168 --> 00:00:50.392
And findings, remembered between sessions.

18
00:00:51.249 --> 00:00:56.924
To measure it, we ran 884 agents on
one Python repository of 86 files.

19
00:00:57.184 --> 00:00:59.710
Three questions, graded
against the syntax tree.

20
00:00:59.968 --> 00:01:06.186
Three models: Claude Haiku 5.5,
Claude Sonnet 5.5 and Claude Opus 5.5.

21
00:01:06.446 --> 00:01:11.162
14 ways to find code, fewest tokens
first. The most reliable is marked.

22
00:01:11.422 --> 00:01:17.147
Against no index: 28% to 54% fewer
tokens, across 4 comparisons.

23
00:01:17.407 --> 00:01:21.631
The most reliable was fully correct
in every run, on both question sets.

24
00:01:22.951 --> 00:01:27.056
The limits are real: one repository,
1 to 6 runs for each setup.

25
00:01:27.456 --> 00:01:29.824
The study measures the
first two things only.

26
00:01:29.968 --> 00:01:32.508
PeterGanuRusty. One command installs it.
